      "text": "Bluff was founded by Mormon pioneers in 1880 during the Hole in the Rock expedition.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.visitutah.com/places-to-go/cities-and-towns/bluff"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name comes from the steep bluffs overlooking the San Juan River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluff%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Bluff’s historic district, the original 1880 townsite, is listed on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://bluffutah.org/town-history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Hole-in-the-Rock trail, which opened into a tributary of Lake Powell, is a key landmark.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bluff%2C_Utah"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Native American tribes such as Paiute, Ute, and Navajo have left petroglyphs and pictographs in the area, evidence of ancient habitation.",
